# Line endings for the files M1 generates.
#
# The generator ALWAYS writes LF (`writeFileSync` with the template's own
# "\n"). The committed blob is LF too. But a Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true hands back CRLF, so the working copy of a GENERATED file
# differs byte-for-byte from what `npm run tokens` produces — and a reviewer
# diffing the working tree sees four "changed" declarations that are only
# line endings (multi-line values such as --font-mono and
# --shadow-overlay-raw). The gates are already line-ending-insensitive (the
# #34 identity freeze hashes CRLF-normalised content, and the M1 sync check
# normalises before comparing), so nothing BREAKS without this file; what this
# file removes is the false alarm.
#
# SCOPED, not repo-wide, on purpose. `* text=auto` would rewrite the 342
# CRLF lines already committed in govee-bulb-issues.md — a change to a file
# this wave does not touch, and a large one. This attribute covers only the
# two generated files, so no committed blob changes: the blob is already LF
# and `text` normalises to LF in the repository. Only the working copy's
# ending changes, and only for these two paths.
webui/app/src/styles/tokens.css text eol=lf
webui/app/src/lib/motion.ts text eol=lf
